ASSIGNMENT OPERATOR:

       An Assignment operator is used to assign (to store) a value into a variable.

Example: 
   int a = 20

  a += 10   (or) a = a + 10  //30
  a -= 5    (or) a = a - 5   //15
  a *= 2    (or) a = a * 2   //40
  a /= 5    (or) a = a / 5   //4
  a %= 3    (or) a = a % 3   //2
